1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Reverse Words in a String — LeetCode 151

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:05,600
Problem: reverse the order of the words in a string, trimming any extra spaces.

3
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:10,000
Input "  the sky is  blue " with messy spaces becomes "blue is sky the".

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Three clean steps: tokenize, reverse, join.

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Step one: pull out the words. A string stream's >> skips every run of whitespace for you.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:22,000
So the leading, trailing, and double spaces just disappear — you get four clean word tiles.

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Step two: reverse the list. The end words swap inward: the with blue, sky with is.

8
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Now the order reads blue, is, sky, the.

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Step three: glue them back together with a single space between each.

10
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,500
The result is "blue is sky the".

11
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:42,500
Bonus, cleaner code: read each word and prepend it — the order flips itself, no vector or reverse.

12
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:47,000
Time O(n); an in-place double reverse gets you O(1) space.

13
